A||||8||Sophia Nova||My red fury||||7||
Z||000000||Sophia Nova||10-28-2001||11:31 AM||||Hi, everyone I'm new to the club and just bought a 1988 base coupe--the red fury :-)   It has 182,000+ miles on it, and I'm contemplating a small block chevy 350 swap.  I have one located and am wondering what the average price of installation would be  (there is now way I can do this myself), and about how many miles max. i should be looking for on the 350?  I drive a lot approx. 100 miles/daily, and refuse to take a plane anywhere I go. Also, I plan on installing some behind-the-seat subwoofers--has anyone done this before, and if so, how did it work out?  I'm a total newbie to the Fiero subculture and am just looking for a little advice here and there.  Thank you all so much!<BR>Sophia Nova ||||reg||7
Z||000001||fix||10-28-2001||12:00 PM||||Welcome to the forum.  First off, v8 swaps aren't cheap.  If you do it yourself you can usually get away with spending about $4000, but if you have someone do it for you the price will be significantly greater.  If you're going to be driving 100 miles a day I would probably go with a mild v8 crate motor because you can still get near 20mpg, and you can buy them for around $1400 new.  However, if it's a very powerful motor that you seek then be prepared to drop even more cash.  A good place to learn about V8 swaps, if you haven't already looked is, <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>www.v8archie.com</A>    <BR><P>------------------<BR>"If it doesn't scare you, it's not fast enough."||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||10-28-2001||01:21 PM||||As far as the gehind the seat woofer thing goes, sure it can be done. If you are no taller then about 5'6", it should be a breeze in truck boxes behind the seats. If you would like to retain the full travel of the seats, you may want to come up with a deifferent option. Here's what I used.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://pip.pennock.nl/uploads/pffinterior.jpg"> <BR>I'm 6'6", so any behind the seat option would not work for me. There are some very nice enclosures available commercially that replace the center console and hold a 10" woofer. And believe me, if you use a quality sub and a quality amp, one 10" sub can be MORE then enough.||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||10-28-2001||07:38 PM||||If I was driving over 100 miles a day, I wouldn't want a V8 for it. Just my opinion.<P>Hey stimp, do passengers ever hesitate to take a ride once they see the "red bottle" in front of them?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">              <BR>^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 SC 2.5L 5spd</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroKyle||10-28-2001||08:07 PM||||Contact Archie on this forum or through E-mail. He is the best expert on V-8s in Fieros. If your driving that much in a day with a v-8 Fiero, your gonna suck a lot of gas and with all that power, sh#t can hit the fan easy. I suggest you get a 2m4 for your daily driving and set aside another Fiero for your v-8 project. I have hard enough time just controlling by 85 GT in the wet without getting sideways and crap. If your driving a V8 Fiero everyday, your gonna have stuff break all the time because the Fiero isn't really made to have 350 hp, but it is still reliable even though its costly. I highly don't reccomend a V-8 Fiero for driving purposes. If ya still want a more powerful daily driver, I suggest a 3800 II with a supercharger. Just my 2 cents and then some.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0PgAgVMwT!1W9RUb20vChbvv6QaE!2K1LWrFB6SxTnTchZgvIygv7Y3YwXpVdD8GeNkWpurYfoQxvNRK6j6kEmOFLoIHavbIr/Kyle-85-GT.jpg">    <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroKyle||10-28-2001||08:09 PM||||If you drive 100 miles a day though, your gonna go much faster though with the V-8, lol. Sounds like your really gonna put some money into having it be a pretty neat little car.||||reg||1
Z||000006||3.8T Fiero GT||10-28-2001||08:29 PM||||HI!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>350 is awesome power and sound!  if u want sumptin easier go 3800 SC!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Hartz||10-29-2001||08:16 AM||||Hey, welcome to the forum.  Always nice to see more Michigan folks.  If you want to check out a V8, shoot me an e-mail - there are a couple around the area here.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Speaking of which, I don't know if I'll have my V8 car put back together in time for tonight's Michigan Fiero Club meeting or not, (I keep telling mysef - less computer time, more garage time...) but you might consider stopping by - lots of neat cars and interesting chat.<P>Take care, good luck,<P>Hartz<P>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>hartzfeld.home.mindspring.com||||reg||1
Z||000008||ChopTop||10-29-2001||08:26 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/</A> <P>You may want to check out the above link and join the Michigan Fiero Club.  You get a monthly newsletter and its a good resource to meet other Fiero enthusiast.  Good luck on your project.||||reg||1
